{
 "title": "When Demand Rises",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "Market Axes",
   "say": "Let's draw a market graph with Price on the vertical axis and Quantity on the horizontal axis.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "main_title",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "What happens when demand rises?",
     "size": 52,
     "color": "ink",
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "axis_y",
     "x1": 200,
     "y1": 750,
     "x2": 200,
     "y2": 180,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "axis_x",
     "x1": 200,
     "y1": 750,
     "x2": 900,
     "y2": 750,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p",
     "x": 60,
     "y": 170,
     "text": "Price\n(P)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q",
     "x": 760,
     "y": 775,
     "text": "Quantity (Q)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Supply and Demand",
   "say": "Here is our upward-sloping Supply curve S, and our initial downward-sloping Demand curve D1.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_s",
     "x1": 260,
     "y1": 690,
     "x2": 760,
     "y2": 190,
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_s",
     "x": 775,
     "y": 170,
     "text": "S (Supply)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_d1",
     "x1": 260,
     "y1": 290,
     "x2": 660,
     "y2": 690,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_d1",
     "x": 675,
     "y": 675,
     "text": "D1",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Initial Equilibrium",
   "say": "Where Supply and Demand meet is the initial equilibrium E1, giving us price P1 and quantity Q1.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "pt_e1",
     "cx": 460,
     "cy": 490,
     "rx": 9,
     "ry": 9,
     "color": "ink",
     "fill": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_e1",
     "x": 465,
     "y": 430,
     "text": "E1",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_p1",
     "x1": 200,
     "y1": 490,
     "x2": 460,
     "y2": 490,
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 3,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_q1",
     "x1": 460,
     "y1": 490,
     "x2": 460,
     "y2": 750,
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 3,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p1",
     "x": 135,
     "y": 472,
     "text": "P1",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q1",
     "x": 440,
     "y": 765,
     "text": "Q1",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Demand Shifts Right",
   "say": "When demand rises, consumers want more at every price, shifting the demand curve right from D1 to D2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_d2",
     "x1": 420,
     "y1": 210,
     "x2": 820,
     "y2": 610,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_d2",
     "x": 835,
     "y": 595,
     "text": "D2 (Higher Demand)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "shift_arr1",
     "x1": 360,
     "y1": 370,
     "x2": 490,
     "y2": 300,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "shift_arr2",
     "x1": 560,
     "y1": 570,
     "x2": 690,
     "y2": 500,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "note_shift",
     "x": 980,
     "y": 220,
     "text": "1. Demand rises\n   (D1 shifts right to D2)",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Shortage at Old Price",
   "say": "At the old price P1, consumers now want QD, which is much more than Q1. This creates a temporary shortage.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "ext_p1",
     "x1": 460,
     "y1": 490,
     "x2": 700,
     "y2": 490,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 3,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "pt_qd",
     "cx": 700,
     "cy": 490,
     "rx": 8,
     "ry": 8,
     "color": "red",
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_qd",
     "x1": 700,
     "y1": 490,
     "x2": 700,
     "y2": 750,
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 3,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_qd",
     "x": 680,
     "y": 765,
     "text": "QD",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "br_shortage",
     "x1": 470,
     "y1": 525,
     "x2": 690,
     "y2": 525,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4,
     "arrow": "both"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_shortage",
     "x": 580,
     "y": 540,
     "text": "Shortage",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "note_short",
     "x": 980,
     "y": 350,
     "text": "2. At P1, a shortage\n   pushes price up",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "New Equilibrium",
   "say": "Competition among buyers bids the price up until we reach the new equilibrium E2, with a higher price P2 and higher quantity Q2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "erase",
     "ids": [
      "ext_p1",
      "pt_qd",
      "dash_qd",
      "lbl_qd",
      "br_shortage",
      "lbl_shortage"
     ]
    },
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "pt_e2",
     "cx": 580,
     "cy": 370,
     "rx": 9,
     "ry": 9,
     "color": "red",
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_e2",
     "x": 575,
     "y": 310,
     "text": "E2",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_p2",
     "x1": 200,
     "y1": 370,
     "x2": 580,
     "y2": 370,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 3,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_q2",
     "x1": 580,
     "y1": 370,
     "x2": 580,
     "y2": 750,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 3,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p2",
     "x": 135,
     "y": 352,
     "text": "P2",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q2",
     "x": 560,
     "y": 765,
     "text": "Q2",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "arr_p_up",
     "x1": 115,
     "y1": 465,
     "x2": 115,
     "y2": 395,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "arr_q_up",
     "x1": 495,
     "y1": 785,
     "x2": 550,
     "y2": 785,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Conclusion",
   "say": "In summary, holding supply constant, when demand rises, both the equilibrium price and quantity increase!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sum_box",
     "x": 960,
     "y": 500,
     "w": 560,
     "h": 240,
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_title",
     "x": 990,
     "y": 525,
     "text": "Conclusion:",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "blue",
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_p",
     "x": 990,
     "y": 590,
     "text": "• Equilibrium Price RISES (P1 -> P2)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_q",
     "x": 990,
     "y": 655,
     "text": "• Equilibrium Quantity RISES (Q1 -> Q2)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}